# Walked twin of unit_a3_caller_binding.lm2 (--walk-methods: its methods are walked).
# Reading 1 (book, "Dynamic sources and the lexical fallback"; Codex, 2026-09-28): a free name of a returned method
# takes the caller's own binding first; the node's copied lexical context is only the fallback.  add5 copied n 5 at
# makeAdder's return.  The root, with its own n 100, calls add5(1): 101.  go, with its formal n 7: 8.  plain, with no
# n of its own: the copy, 6.  Success is 7; otherwise 64 plus a bit per failed reading.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN

add5: makeAdder 5
fn: go (int: n) int
    return: add5: 1
fn: plain () int
    return: add5: 1
int: n 100
int: a (add5: 1)
int: b (go: 7)
int: c (plain())
int: bad 0
if: a != 101
    bad: bad + 1
if: b != 8
    bad: bad + 2
if: c != 6
    bad: bad + 4
int: ok 7
if: bad != 0
    ok: 64 + bad
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
